From 500d0a1bc63e868695f6cbaff9091da44e7040c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:32:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] perf(kernel): instrument the step import stages

Tracing-only timings with the stable stage names (parse, topology,
build, mesh_plan, mesh_deviation, weld, facets) on the STEP read path,
the machining-mesh plan/measure/evaluate/weld path and the per-solid
mesh loop. A new ignored release-lane bench row reads the #4200 repro
rotor from CAMCRAFT_ROTOR_STEP and prints the timings; without the file
it skips. No behaviour or verdict changes.

The rotor profile: read ~20 s; the mesh stages dominate (mesh_deviation
115-167 s per attempt over 88-95M samples; mesh_plan 18-65 s), and the
0.005 mm attempt plus the loose-chord 0.01 mm path is ~640 s of work,
past the 300 s bound.

Refs #4200
